{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"**Yes.** Under Irish CBI UCITS Q&A 1088, listed ETF and unlisted non-ETF classes may coexist within the same UCITS/sub-fund. The prospectus must clearly compare their material differences, including:\n\n- **Dealing:** exchange trading versus direct subscriptions/redemptions; dealing frequency, cut-offs and procedures.\n- **Settlement:** applicable settlement periods and arrangements.\n- **Costs:** class fees and expenses, subscription/redemption charges, brokerage, spreads and other transaction costs, where applicable.\n- **Minimums:** minimum subscriptions, holdings and redemption amounts, as applicable.\n- **Rights:** rights attaching to each class, particularly access to direct redemption.\n- **Liquidity:** secondary-market liquidity versus fund-dealing availability, including relevant restrictions.\n- **Price:** ETF exchange prices versus NAV-based dealing prices, including potential premiums/discounts to NAV.\n\n**Worth knowing:** This is an Irish disclosure framework—not US share-class exemptive relief. US-specific operational conditions should not be imported."}}
